  "body": "Found by the release QA swarm (#2582) on **v0.24.0** (Linux tarball), driven through `camcraft-cli mcp` by a Codex agent. Part: 120 x 80 x 12 mm plate, 4 outside R6 corners, Tormach 770MX.\n\n## What happens\nA 2D Contour around the outside, Ø10 flat end mill, stepdown 3, 4 tabs (3 wide x 1 high), with the **default** lead (`lead: {linear: {length: 8}}`), generates with status `ok`, but verify holds the post:\n\n```\nfeed moves 5 and 13 cross in XY at shared depth\nfeed moves 20 and 28 cross in XY at shared depth\nfeed moves 35 and 43 cross in XY at shared depth\nfeed moves 50 and 58 cross in XY at shared depth\n```\nOne crossing per depth level (4 levels). With `lead: \"none\"` the crossings go away and the program posts.\n\n## Expected\nThe default lead on an ordinary outside contour with tabs makes a path that verifies, or generation refuses with a reason. Either the lead-in/lead-out (or the tab gap moves) really cross the cut, or the crossing law convicts a harmless lead. The run did not establish which.\n\n## Reproduce\nOn skull: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/q01-blocked.camproj` -> `open_project`, `generate {name:\"Outside\"}`, `verify {name:\"Outside\"}`. Full calls: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/evidence.jsonl` steps 42, 44, 63-67; report `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/REPORT.md` (P2).\n\nNot checked on current main.\n\nDone means: an outside 2D Contour with tabs and the default lead verifies and posts on this part (or is refused at generate with a named reason), pinned by a test.\n",
